  "articleSummary": "**Summary:**\n\n* **Core Thesis:** The primary AI security threat is not a single superintelligent breakthrough, but the compounding multiplication of two ordinary curves: agent endurance (task length) and breadth (orchestrated sub-agents). \n* **Key Technologies & Concepts:** Discusses autonomous AI agents, orchestrators (e.g., Claude Code), METR's time-horizon benchmarks, and \"LLMjacking\" (where attackers use stolen cloud credentials to run free, automated swarm attacks charged to the victim).\n* **Tone & Framing:** Written as a pragmatic, slightly cynical analysis/warning, utilizing *The Terminator* (\"absolutely will not stop\") as a recurring metaphor for relentless, automated compute consumption.\n* **Intended Audience:** Software engineering teams, security professionals, and technical decision-makers who dismiss current agentic threats as hype.",
